{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall command, and slaughter.</b> The commanding is by the priest, and the slaughter by any person." "<b>And slaughter the one bird.</b> The choicer of the two." "<b>Over living water.</b> To say that the dead person — that is, the leper, who is considered as dead — now mingles with the living, to enter the camp and be like other people. Over living water — to mingle with the blood, for the blood itself is not sufficient to dip into it the cedar wood and the scarlet thread and the hyssop."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:08.349822086Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}